BT 1 0 0 1 0 75.1 Tm 15 0 Td .841903 Tw /F2+0 10.7 Tf 14.3 TL (In Part I, we analyzed individual decision making, both in abstract decision problems) Tj T* 0 Tw -15 0 Td -0.108766 Tw (and in more specific economic settings. Our primary aim was to lay the groundwork for the) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.092314 Tw (study of how the simultaneous behavior of many self-interested individuals \(including) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.079199 Tw (firms\) generates economic outcomes in market economies. Most of the remainder of the) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.441294 Tw (book is devoted to this task. In Part II, however, we study in a more general way how) Tj T* 0 Tw (multiperson interactions can be modeled.) Tj T* ET
