BT 1 0 0 1 0 118 Tm 15 0 Td .071819 Tw 14.3 TL 0 0 0 rg /F2+0 10.7 Tf 14.3 TL (A central feature of multiperson interaction is the potential for the presence of ) Tj /F4+0 10.7 Tf 14.3 TL (strategic) Tj T* 0 Tw -15 0 Td .62805 Tw (interdependence) Tj /F2+0 10.7 Tf 14.3 TL (. In our study of individual decision making in Part I, the decision maker) Tj T* 0 Tw .354361 Tw (faced situations in which her well-being depended only on the choices she made \(possibly) Tj T* 0 Tw 7.309071 Tw (with some randomness\). In contrast, in multiperson situations with strategic) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.032613 Tw (interdependence, each agent recognizes that the payoff she receives \(in utility or profits\)) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.751195 Tw (depends not only on her own actions but also on the actions of other individuals. The) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.259385 Tw (actions that are best for her to take may depend on actions these other individuals have) Tj T* 0 Tw .272518 Tw (already taken, on those she expects them to be taking at the same time, and even on future) Tj T* 0 Tw (actions that they may take, or decide not to take, as a result of her current actions.) Tj T* ET
