BT 1 0 0 1 0 60.8 Tm 15 0 Td 4.567116 Tw 14.3 TL 0 0 0 rg /F2+0 10.7 Tf 14.3 TL (The tool that we use for analyzing settings with strategic interdependence is) Tj T* 0 Tw -15 0 Td 3.094265 Tw /F4+0 10.7 Tf 14.3 TL (noncooperative game theory) Tj /F2+0 10.7 Tf 14.3 TL (. Although the term \001game\002 may seem to undersell the) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.178733 Tw (theory's importance, it correctly highlights the theory's central feature: The agents under) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.581836 Tw (study are concerned with strategy and winning \(in the general sense of utility or profit) Tj T* 0 Tw (maximization\) in much the same way that players of most parlor games are.) Tj T* ET
