BT 1 0 0 1 0 103.7 Tm 15 0 Td 4.398965 Tw 14.3 TL 0 0 0 rg /F2+0 10.7 Tf 14.3 TL (Multiperson economic situations vary greatly in the degree to which strategic) Tj T* 0 Tw -15 0 Td .285632 Tw (interaction is present. In settings of monopoly \(where a good is sold by only a single firm;) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.242749 Tw (see Section 12.B\) or of perfect competition \(where all agents act as price takers; see) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.603108 Tw (Chapter 10 and Part IV\), the nature of strategic interaction is minimal enough that our) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.041751 Tw (analysis need not make any formal use of game theory.) Tj 5.35 Ts /F2+0 8.7 Tf 14.3 TL (1) Tj 0 Ts /F2+0 10.7 Tf 14.3 TL ( In other settings, however, such as) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.962113 Tw (the analysis of oligopolistic markets \(where there is more than one but still not many) Tj T* 0 Tw .090117 Tw (sellers of a good; see Sections 12.C to 12.G\), the central role of strategic interaction makes) Tj T* 0 Tw (game theory indispensable for our analysis.) Tj T* ET
